## Status

Self-excluded: **no verified public benchmark numbers** were found for the exact model/ID `gemini-2.5-pro` in accessible sources at time of research.

## Research notes

- Verified metadata from accessible sources (not benchmark scores): Google AI docs list `gemini-2.5-pro` as a deprecated thinking model (knowledge cutoff Jan 2025, 1,048,576 input / 65,536 output token limits) supporting audio/image/video/text/PDF inputs and text output, with capabilities including thinking, function calling, code execution, grounding, caching, structured outputs, and tool use. Artificial Analysis lists Gemini 2.5 Pro as a proprietary reasoning model (released 2025-06-05) with 1M context, multimodal inputs, and pricing around $1.25/$10.00 per 1M tokens in the fetched snapshot. OpenRouter lists `google/gemini-2.5-pro`.
- Artificial Analysis reported Intelligence Index and task-level benchmark aggregates as unavailable/N/A in the fetched snapshot. Public benchmark claims for Gemini 2.5 Pro exist historically, but no extractable verified benchmark numbers for this exact model/ID were captured from the accessible fetched sources in this session (docs/aggregator pages did not provide numeric benchmark results in text).
- Per `model-report-TEMPLATE.md`: if zero verified public benchmark numbers are found for the exact model/ID, save a notes-only `.md.excluded` file and do not invent placeholder scores.

